ok nothing is built before the first request
ok a GET answers the handler's status and body
ok the headers are lower-case and carry the body's byte length
ok a POST body reaches the form decoder
ok a redirect keeps its location header
ok HEAD sends no body but the GET's content-length
ok an unknown path is the dispatcher's 404
ok a verb the path does not route is 405 with Allow
ok a request without rack.input is served
ok one process builds the dispatcher once
ok a forked child builds its own dispatcher
ok the parent keeps the one it had
